{
  "name": "Crunchyroll's season 1 holds both cours, episodes 1 to 11 and 12 to 23",
  "source": {
    "file": "docs/src/content/docs/design/representation.md",
    "test": "section 8.1, Mushoku Tensei, the fold end to end"
  },
  "why": "One Crunchyroll season is two broadcast runs. Cour 1 aired 11 episodes from 2021-01-10 and cour 2 aired 12 from 2021-10-03, nine months later, and Crunchyroll sells both as season 1 with a special, 24 rows. The season is therefore neither run: it HOLDS them, its rows 1 to 11 are cour 1's 1 to 11 and its rows 12 to 23 are cour 2's 1 to 12, which is the only reading under which every episode is itself. The record: \"Emits eleven EPISODE_LINK and INCLUDES(cr season 1 to anilist:108465, fromStart 1, fromEnd 11, toStart 1, toEnd 11, contiguous, aligned 11, total 24) ... The same pass on cour 2's cluster pairs their 12 to 23 with cour 2's 1 to 12\". The special pairs with nothing, because nothing else is that episode. Netflix season 1 is 24 positional placeholders with no titles and no dates, and unogs refused the ask, so no claim exists and nothing may be minted from it: it stays a badge.",
